title: Party Disunity
new-page: true
view-if: player_party = "erc" and erc_disunity_timer = 0 and (erc_dissent >= 30 or (erc_left_dissent > 30) or (erc_core_dissent > 30) or (erc_civic_dissent > 30) or (erc_pragmatic_dissent > 30))
on-arrival: month_actions += 1 if not erc_advisor_action or difficulty >= 0; erc_disunity_timer = 4
card-image: img/erc/disunity.jpeg
face-image: img/erc/disunity.jpeg
frequency: 200
tags: erc_party jxsi_party jxcat_party
role: card-party

= Party Disunity

The party is being torn apart by internal dissent. Upset at the leadership and general direction, factions have started sabotaging their rivals, hampering our efforts to win votes and carry out our policies.

[? if erc_civic_dissent > 30 : Our ties with civil society organizations are strained due to recent party decisions.  ?]
[? if erc_pragmatic_dissent > 30 : The pragmatic wing is displeased with the direction of our party. ?]
[? if erc_core_dissent > 30 : The republican core of our party feels says we're betraying our principles. ?]
[? if erc_left_dissent > 30: The left wing is quite unhappy with our course of action. ?]

Something must be done to reinforce party unity.

# TBD: Add these? I believe they make more sense only as advisor action, but let's see
# - @mediate
# - @defend_agreement
# - @social_agreement

- @enforce_unity
- @concessions_civic
- @concessions_pragmatics
- @concessions_core
- @concessions_left
- @do_nothing
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@enforce_unity
title: Enforce party discipline.
on-arrival: {!
    Q.erc_civic_dissent -= 8; Q.erc_pragmatic_dissent -= 8; Q.erc_core_dissent -= 8; Q.erc_left_dissent -= 8;

    var target = "erc";
    var targetCongreso = "erc";
    var targetLocal = "erc";
    if (Q.erc_in_jxsi) {
        target = "jxsi";
        if (Q.jxsi_in_congreso) {
            targetCongreso = "jxsi";
        }
        if (Q.jxsi_in_local) {
            targetLocal = "jxsi";
        }
    } else if (Q.erc_in_jxcat) {
        target = "jxcat";
        if (Q.jxcat_in_congreso) {
            targetCongreso = "jxcat";
        }
        if (Q.jxcat_in_local) {
            targetLocal = "jxcat";
        }
    }
    

    var dissentScale = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, Q.erc_dissent / 100));
    var disciplineLoss = {
        middle: 3.5 * dissentScale,
        ind: 1.5 * dissentScale,
        rural: 1.5 * dissentScale,
        young: 1.5 * dissentScale,
        unemployed: 1.0 * dissentScale
    };
    for (var demographic in disciplineLoss) {
        var loss = disciplineLoss[demographic];
        G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, { contest: "parlament", to: "abstain", from: target, amount: loss * 0.6, maxDonorFraction: 0.5, constituencies: "all", demographics: [demographic] });
        if (!Q["cup_in_" + target]) {
            G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, { contest: "parlament", to: "cup", from: target, amount: loss * 0.2, maxDonorFraction: 0.5, constituencies: "all", demographics: [demographic] });
        }
        G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, { contest: "parlament", to: "federal_left", from: target, amount: loss * 0.2, maxDonorFraction: 0.5, constituencies: "all", demographics: [demographic] });
    }
    G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, { contest: "congreso", to: "abstain", from: targetCongreso, amount: 0.5 * dissentScale, maxDonorFraction: 0.5, constituencies: ["catalunya"] });
    G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, { contest: "congreso", to: "federal_left", from: targetCongreso, amount: 0.25 * dissentScale, maxDonorFraction: 0.5, constituencies: ["catalunya"] });
    G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, { contest: "barcelona", to: "bcomu", from: targetLocal, amount: 0.3 * dissentScale, maxDonorFraction: 0.5 });
    G.cardSupportTransfer(Q, { contest: "barcelona", to: "psc", from: targetLocal, amount: 0.2 * dissentScale, maxDonorFraction: 0.5 });
    Q.erc_redbelt_mod = Math.max(-10, Q.erc_redbelt_mod - 0.5 * dissentScale);
    Q.erc_interior_mod = Math.max(-5, Q.erc_interior_mod - 0.5 * dissentScale);
!}

Enforcing party discipline reduces dissent, but it could lead to an exit of dissenting members.

@concessions_civic
title: Give concessions to the civil organizations.
view-if: erc_civic_dissent > 30
on-arrival: erc_civic_dissent -= 15; erc_pragmatic_dissent += 10

We have promised to follow through with our promises to many civil society organizations. The pragmatic wing of our party is bickering about it not being very realistic.

@concessions_core
title: Give concessions to our republican core.
view-if: erc_core_dissent > 30
on-arrival: erc_core_dissent -= 15; erc_left_dissent += 8; erc_pragmatic_dissent += 8;

We have promised to take more policy suggestions from the republican core. Both the left and pragmatic wings of the party might be displeased.

@concessions_left
title: Give concessions to the left.
view-if: erc_left_dissent > 30
on-arrival: erc_left_dissent -= 15; erc_pragmatic_dissent += 5; erc_core_dissent += 5

We have promised that we will listen to the left wing of the party. Of course, this leads to increased dissent from the pragmatics and the republican core.

@concessions_pragmatics
title: Give concessions to the pragmatics.
view-if: erc_pragmatic_dissent > 30
on-arrival: erc_pragmatic_dissent -= 15; erc_left_dissent += 5; erc_civic_dissent += 10;

We have promised to follow the path of pragmatism and Realpolitik a bit closer from now on. This upsets the civic organizations and the left wing of our party, for they believe that values should always come first.


@do_nothing
title: Let the factions argue with themselves.
on-arrival: erc_pragmatic_dissent += 1; erc_left_dissent += 1; erc_core_dissent += 1; erc_civic_dissent += 1

Let the factions bicker; perhaps dissent is healthy for the party.


# TODO: Add expel actions?

@mediate
title: Mediate between the party's factions
view-if: oriol_junqueras_advisor
choose-if: oriol_junqueras_advisor
on-arrival: {!        
    for (var faction of ["left", "core", "pragmatic", "civic"]) Q["erc_" + faction + "_dissent"] = Math.max(0, Q["erc_" + faction + "_dissent"] - 4);
!}

Oriol Junqueras has done his best to bring the factions together. While it's inevitable that some disagreements remain, at least people seem more willing to tolerate them.

- @post_event: Let's hope this is enough!

@defend_agreement
title: Defend the current governing agreement
view-if: (oriol_junqueras_advisor or roger_torrent_advisor or carles_mundo_advisor) and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)
choose-if: (oriol_junqueras_advisor or roger_torrent_advisor or carles_mundo_advisor) and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting)
on-arrival: {!
    var relief = Q.burdens_broken || Q.broken_roadmap ? 1 : 4;
    for (var faction of ["left", "core", "pragmatic", "civic"]) Q["erc_" + faction + "_dissent"] = Math.max(0, Q["erc_" + faction + "_dissent"] - relief);
!}

The agreement has been defended inside the party, and some may have been somewhat convinced. [? if burdens_broken or broken_roadmap: Nonetheless, our broken promises will still require actual action to mend any scars left behind... ?]

- @post_event: Continue...

@social_agreement
title: Defend the social commitments of the current government
view-if: dolors_bassa_advisor and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting) and burdens_time > 0 and not burdens_broken
choose-if: dolors_bassa_advisor and (erc_in_gob or erc_supporting) and burdens_time > 0 and not burdens_broken
on-arrival: {!
    Q.erc_left_dissent = Math.max(0, Q.erc_left_dissent - 6); Q.erc_core_dissent = Math.max(0, Q.erc_core_dissent - 2);
!}

Dolors Bassa has made the case for pursuing the agreement's social commitments. 

- @post_event: Now it's up to us to deliver them!

